---
description: Enforce D-drive and repo-local storage for nar
alwaysApply: true
---

# Storage and Path Policy

- Never read or write `nar` artifacts, caches, datasets, builds, or dependencies on `C:`.
- Keep all `nar` state under `D:/data/nar`.
- Use repo-local paths:
  - `third_party/ns-3-dev` for ns-3 source (git submodule)
  - `artifacts/<topic>/...` for runtime traces and results
  - `topics/<topic>/infra/baselines` for baseline metrics
- Do not hardcode user-specific absolute paths (especially under `C:/Users/...`).
- Prefer paths relative to repository root so all users can run the project consistently.
